                <pb facs="0141" n="65" sameAs="frus:frus1935v02/pg65"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">611.4331/58: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Consul General at St.
                        John’s</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Quarton</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1935-04-16T18:00:00-05:00">April 16, 1935—6 p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Your April 9, 5 p.m. Consideration is being given to the question of announcing
                    intention to negotiate with Newfoundland. Upon determination thereof you will be
                    informed.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
